  "notes": "Transcribed from the official SCC 'Commercial Music, Music Business Management Emphasis A.A. Degree - Cal-GETC GE' program map, Catalog 2026-27, published August 15, 2026 (mapmaker.losrios.edu/Maps/7785/PublishedPdf). GE Pattern: Cal-GETC. Official Total Units: 61-62; this seed models the first-listed/recommended low path = 15 + 15 + 15 + 16 = 61 units (ENGL C1000 at 3 units per the official SCC English course page). Semester sums verified against the map's 15-16 / 15 / 15 / 16 headers. 4 terms (within the AA/AS 4-7 gate). Choice slots — Major Elective (minimum 12 units, at least 1 course from each group): (1) Sem 1 ME *Major Elective - Business Management (3) — ACCT 101 Fundamentals of Accounting selected (first-listed, 3 units); (2) Sem 2 ME *Major Elective - Communication Skills (3) — COMM C1004 Interpersonal Communications selected (first-listed, 3 units); (3) Sem 3 ME *Major Elective - Retail Marketing (3) — MKT 300 Principles of Marketing selected (first-listed, 3 units); (4) Sem 4 ME *Major Elective - Any Group (3) — MGMT 308 Personnel & Human Resources Management selected (first-listed remaining Business Management option, 3 units); total 12 units with at least 1 from each group (Business Management, Communication Skills, Retail Marketing). (5) GE ENGL C1000 / 488 / H+ ESLW 340 +, Area 1A — ENGL C1000 selected; all other slots are fixed. ME-list notes: CISA 305 (2 units) and CISA 340 (2 units) require an additional course from ANY area to complete 12 units (not selected); CISA 305 requires CISC 300 or 310 (not selected); COMM 331 & 361 require ENGL C1000 or ESLW 340 (in plan, but not selected). Documented prerequisites: MUSM 115 requires MUSM 110 (in plan). Students not placing directly in ENGL C1000 take the ENGL 80/ENGL C1000 combo; ENGL 488 requires ESL 325; ESLW 340 requires ESL 325 or Los Rios assessment placement. Students not placing directly in MATH 300 take the MATHS 95/MATH 300 combo. MUFHL 309 fills Cal-GETC Area 3A. Area 4 rule: the Sem 4 Area 4 course must be from a different discipline than the Sem 1 Area 4 course. GE Area 5C: the 1-unit Associate Lab Component is not required if a laboratory activity is included in the Area 5A or 5B course (per map note); modeled here as a generic 1-unit Area 5C slot. AA/AS requirements: 60 degree-applicable units with 2.0 GPA, 12 units within Los Rios, each required course 'C' or better, Cal-GETC Areas 1-6 with 'C' or better. Bachelor's-degree holders are deemed to have satisfied GE/graduation competency (per map). Music - Commercial Music, Music Business Management Emphasis, Arts & Communication Meta Majors. tccns mirrors SCC local course codes (California community colleges do not use TCCNS).",
